🔼 1) Upload File for ITR
POST /api/itr/upload
Uploads an attachment for ITR and returns a path you can store in your JSON fields (like drawingattach, attachtest, etc.)
Request Type
multipart/form-data
Form Field
Field
Type
Required
file
file
✅

Success Response (200)
{
  "filePath": "/uploads/itr/170687123123-123456789.pdf"
}

Error Response (400)
{
  "error": "No file uploaded"
}

✅ Note: This API only returns the file path; it does not create an ITR.

